1
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,640
CAI RONGGEN

2
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:16,440
Hello, everyone.

3
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:20,040
I'm Zheng Yu, from Qing Yi University's
College of Life Sciences.

4
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:30,680
As we all know, aluminum adjuvants
usually deliver antigens

5
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:33,200
by attaching to the surface
of cell membranes.

6
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:34,720
They don't enter the cells themselves,

7
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:38,720
so they can't participate in intracellular
antigen processing and presentation.

8
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,520
Due to this drawback,

9
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:41,960
in practical applications,

10
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:45,800
using them alone doesn't provide
comprehensive protection for the body.

11
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:49,320
Our project proposes
modifying traditional aluminum adjuvants

12
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:51,360
by converting them into a particulate form

13
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:54,440
to improve their ability
to induce cellular immunity.

14
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,080
That concludes our presentation.

15
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,680
Ms. Zheng Yu,

16
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:45,240
how safe is this particulate aluminum
adjuvant emulsion?

17
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:49,320
Aluminum adjuvants are currently the only
adjuvants approved for clinical use.

18
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:51,760
And the raw materials for this emulsion

19
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,640
are clinically approved squalene
and aluminum adjuvants.

20
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,760
It is exceptionally safe.

21
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:59,760
We've also conducted
corresponding experiments to verify this.

22
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:00,720
I have a question.

23
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,440
Emulsion particles are relatively large.

24
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:05,400
Wouldn't this affect the endocytosis
by antigen-presenting cells?

25
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:08,720
By adding the particles to
the oil emulsion system

26
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,760
and blending them
using the method we chose,

27
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:12,640
we produced uniform particle sizes
of 500 nm.

28
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:15,480
If we can further optimize
preparation conditions,

29
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:18,920
we should be able to produce
an even more optimal particle size.

30
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,279
Mr. Cai.

31
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:21,600
Do you have any questions?

32
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:46,000
Let's thank this student
for an excellent presentation.

33
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:50,120
GUIDANCE AND CONSTRUCTIVE CRITICISM
GREATLY APPRECIATED!

34
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:58,840
Next, a team from
The Qing Yi University of Engineering.

35
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,840
Representing their team is

36
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:04,240
Jiang Yingtian, a biotechnology student
from the College of Life Sciences.

37
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:11,760
Hello, respected judges.

38
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:13,560
My name is Jiang Yingtian.

39
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:16,080
I asked some industry veterans

40
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:18,880
who work in this field
to help me collect these photos.

41
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:21,000
With these photos as supporting material,

42
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:23,960
I gained a much clearer understanding
of my project's research direction.

43
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:36,720
Before this, I thought we wouldn't have
any problem winning first prize.

44
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:40,120
But after hearing your presentation,
we might win the grand prize.

45
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:44,320
Now, I might really have to rely on you
to redeem my reputation.

46
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,680
You didn't hear the other presentations.

47
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:53,480
Li Yanan said they were pretty average.

48
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:56,920
There are still plenty of contestants
who haven't presented.

49
00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:00,120
Besides, every judge
has different preferences.

50
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:02,600
I made the images
on one of my slides too small.

51
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,480
I could barely see them on the stage.

52
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:08,240
And I even stumbled over some of my words.

53
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,120
What's wrong with you?

54
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,600
Chen Yanzhou.

55
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:25,360
Honestly, I'm someone

56
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:28,800
who's pretty unlucky most of the time.

57
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:33,800
If we end up empty-handed,

58
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,120
will you be disappointed?

59
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,440
I was wondering
where you two had disappeared to.

60
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:44,960
We came out for some air.

61
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:49,720
Did you come to the finals to compete
with students from other universities,

62
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:53,080
or are you just here
to inspect your teammate's presentation?

63
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:55,240
Here.

64
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,720
THE ORDER OF MOUNTAINS TEA CEREMONY

65
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:58,640
Do I get a prize
just for making it to the finals?

66
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,480
What prize?

67
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:02,200
You put in the wrong address.

68
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:04,560
The stuff you bought online
got delivered to my place.

69
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:09,920
- You bought--
- Let's go.

70
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,640
Let's get back and watch.

71
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:12,960
What's the rush?

72
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:16,640
I'll head inside first. The final results
will be out in three days.

73
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:19,040
Don't overthink things
these next few days.

74
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:23,640
- Let's go.
- Goodness. What's going on now?

75
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,480
We have conducted
long-term safety monitoring.

76
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:34,600
All right, all right.

77
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:36,720
So the main focus is on public education,

78
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:40,680
making a higher level of social awareness
absolutely crucial.

79
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:43,080
Under our professor's guidance,
we're all thinking about

80
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:46,640
what kind of academic contribution is best
to use as our research direction?

81
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:49,880
You should be more careful
when buying things next time.

82
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:53,920
It's all because I helped you snag that
limited-edition fishing rod last time.

83
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Otherwise, I wouldn't have
used your address.

84
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:57,200
Why are you blaming me?

85
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,400
Good thing I did use the wrong address.

86
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:03,080
What?

87
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:05,200
Nothing.

88
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:09,960
I even went out of my way to put it
in a bag for you that said "tea."

89
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:11,640
Give it back to me then.

90
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:19,680
My wife saw this and got the wrong idea,
do you know that?

91
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,840
Why did you buy women's perfume?

92
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:29,280
I bought it to study the ingredients.

93
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,919
Aren't you studying thale cress?

94
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,200
When did you change research topics?

95
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,440
Why do you care so much?

96
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:39,720
Good.

97
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:49,040
THANK YOU

98
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:53,680
What's that?

99
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:57,560
Mind your own business.

100
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,520
All right then.

101
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:06,320
EVALUATION SHEET
EXCELLENCE CUP

102
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:12,440
Mr. Sun, Mr. Cai, we're heading off now.

103
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,120
- All right.
- Take care.

104
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:17,520
Speaking of which,

105
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:20,440
the contestant who impressed me most
was No. 6.

106
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:22,360
The girl from Qing Yi University, right?

107
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,360
Commercial aluminum adjuvants.
It was good.

108
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,120
You wouldn't know she was just a junior.

109
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,080
Everyone thinks so?

110
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:31,360
In that case, the grand prize is
pretty much decided, isn't it?

111
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:33,720
- Mr. Cai.
- Yes?

112
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:36,360
You're the key person here.
What do you think?

113
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:41,080
Knowing Ms. Ye, if she were here,
she'd definitely pick No. 6, right?

114
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,160
And Mr. Cai…

115
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:44,560
Birds of a feather flock together.

116
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:47,000
I'm guessing you'd bet on
No. 6 too, right?

117
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:52,440
No. 6 was certainly impressive.

118
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:54,360
But…

119
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:57,120
I believe No. 7 might be more interesting.

120
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:02,240
I also believe No. 7 was pretty good.

121
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:04,680
As for No. 6, she was solid in content,

122
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:08,680
but her delivery was a little…

123
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:10,800
rigid.

124
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:12,960
How about this?

125
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:15,920
Let's get a copy of the competition
footage and send it to Ms. Ye.

126
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,720
We won't waste too much of her time.

127
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:20,760
We'll just copy the clips
of No. 6 and No. 7

128
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,120
and let her judge them.

129
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,960
How about we make a bet?

130
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,120
Sounds good to me.

131
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:29,080
Anyway…

132
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:32,240
We still have something to attend to,
so we'll get going.

133
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,920
All right, take care.

134
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:38,920
- Mr. Cai.
- Yes?

135
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:42,520
I have a bottle of fine wine
I've been saving at the Jinkairui Hotel.

136
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:45,160
I know you appreciate good wine,
so I'd love for you to try it.

137
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:49,000
I also have some business matters
I'd like to discuss with you.

138
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,760
Let's skip the drinks
if we're talking business.

139
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:55,760
Drinking too much can cause problems.

140
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:57,760
We're all on the same side.

141
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:59,400
If we drink behind closed doors,

142
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:02,680
no one outside will hear about it,
even if anything goes wrong.

143
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:08,000
Look, I really have plans tonight.

144
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:10,760
And for business matters,

145
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:12,680
Ms. Ye Sheng has the final say.

146
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,520
As you've seen,
I don't have much say in this.

147
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:18,320
In that case, regarding the wine…

148
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:20,360
- Let's save it for next time.
- Sure.

149
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,720
I'll get going.

150
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:25,720
Mr. Wu, Mr. Sun.
I'll leave first.

151
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:28,520
- All right. Take care, Mr. Cai.
- See you around!

152
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:43,600
YE SHENG, CHAIRMAN AND CEO
OF NINGSHENG BIOTECH

153
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:02,680
ABOUT NINGSHENG

154
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:03,960
PRODUCTS AND SERVICES

155
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:17,080
This university town
is really full of hidden talent.

156
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,000
Who would've thought

157
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:22,360
that a girl working part-time
at a convenience store

158
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:24,040
was actually a top student?

159
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,040
The final results aren't out yet.

160
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:30,560
As a sponsor's representative,

161
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:33,440
isn't it inappropriate for you
to meet a contestant in private?

162
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:40,680
This isn't the first time
we've met in private, is it?

163
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:44,560
Let me put it this way.

164
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:45,720
I came to see you

165
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:48,200
because I want to make
another deal with you.

166
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:51,240
Another deal?

167
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,160
Compensation is compensation.

168
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:55,520
It has nothing to do with a deal.

169
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,120
Fine.

170
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:05,240
Let's go somewhere else to talk
when you get off work.

171
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:07,800
We'll talk about your competition project.

172
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:16,280
- Boss, can I have some of this?
- What do you think?

173
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:18,240
This is delicious.

174
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:20,080
DRY MALATANG

175
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:24,040
Have some more.

176
00:13:33,360 --> 00:13:34,200
Sit.

177
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:38,720
You get off work this late?

178
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:40,200
How much do you make a day?

179
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:42,960
What exactly do you want?

180
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:50,160
Take out your phone.

181
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:56,080
I'm not like you.

182
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:57,480
I won't record this secretly.

183
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,720
Turn it off.

184
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,320
Withdraw from the competition.

185
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:25,560
As for your reason
for withdrawing, just state that

186
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,440
your project was ghostwritten.

187
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:31,560
Do you think I'd ruin my own future?

188
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,080
It's not as serious as you think.

189
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:37,120
As long as you agree,
I'll give you some compensation.

190
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,600
Why don't you think it over?

191
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:50,600
You don't really think
you'll win that prize money, do you?

192
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:55,040
I can tell you with absolute certainty
that your project won't win a prize.

193
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:58,240
If you really have the power
to keep me from winning,

194
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:00,800
then why are you asking me to withdraw?

195
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:05,040
You're missing the point.

196
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:12,720
My goal

197
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:13,920
isn't to make you withdraw.

198
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:16,240
It's to make you admit
your project is fake.

199
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:20,000
The moment you do that,
I'll transfer 50,000 to you right away.

200
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,080
Fifty thousand.

201
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:31,360
Is my reputation

202
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:33,120
that valuable?

203
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:48,960
Hello.

204
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:50,040
Mr. Cao.

205
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:53,200
About that bottle of wine you mentioned.

206
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,920
I think tonight's the night to open it.

207
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:58,840
<i>Mr. Cai, are you done with your plans?</i>

208
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,280
I just finished up.

209
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:04,440
I'm bringing an extra person tonight.
You don't mind, do you?

210
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:06,280
We can use this chance
to discuss business.

211
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:08,320
<i>May I ask which executive?</i>

212
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:11,120
Boss Jiang.

213
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,440
<i>Jiang?</i>

214
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:16,520
<i>I heard his son is also competing</i>
<i>in the Excellence Cup.</i>

215
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:22,440
There's no rush. Let's talk when we meet.

216
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:46,160
CHEN YANZHOU

217
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:57,840
HELLO, PATIENT JIANG HAIZHEN.

218
00:16:57,920 --> 00:17:01,120
YOU HAVE OUTSTANDING MEDICAL BILLS
TOTALING 1202.01 YUAN.

219
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:20,200
Zheng Yu. You're back.

220
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:26,800
Those two went on a trip. They left
as soon as the competition ended.

221
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:30,600
They said there was still time,
and they didn't want to waste the break.

222
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:44,880
Zheng Yu.

223
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:49,840
You were amazing on stage today.

224
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:53,040
I've never seen you compete
in anything like this before.

225
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:55,360
I watched all the other teams
that presented after you.

226
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:57,000
Your team is definitely winning a prize.

227
00:17:58,400 --> 00:17:59,280
Do you think so?

228
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:25,240
INTEGRATION OF UPSTREAM SIGNALING PATHWAYS
WITH AUTOPHAGY-RELATED PROTEINS

229
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:35,560
THE ORDER OF MOUNTAINS TEA CEREMONY

230
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:47,520
<i>This perfume smells really good.</i>

231
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:49,320
<i>When you first spray it,</i>

232
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:50,840
<i>it smells like the rain.</i>

233
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:53,200
<i>After ten minutes,</i>

234
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:55,280
<i>it transforms into the warmth of sunshine.</i>

235
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:17,120
Which irresponsible person wrote
such nonsense perfume reviews online?

236
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:14,320
Not a chance.

237
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:31,800
THANK YOU

238
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,640
"NingSheng BioTech."

239
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:47,080
Sounds very familiar.

240
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:50,280
YE SHENG, CHAIRMAN AND CEO
OF NINGSHENG BIOTECH

241
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:04,920
EXCELLENCE CUP
COMPETITION OVERVIEW

242
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,840
MULTIPLE RESEARCH DIRECTIONS SHOWCASED

243
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:12,320
<i>The publicity team</i>
<i>even took a solo photo of Zheng Yu.</i>

244
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:25,280
<i>Chen Yanzhou.</i>

245
00:21:25,360 --> 00:21:27,440
<i>Honestly, I'm someone</i>

246
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:29,960
<i>who's pretty unlucky most of the time.</i>

247
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:33,160
<i>If we end up empty-handed,</i>

248
00:21:33,240 --> 00:21:34,760
<i>will you be disappointed?</i>

249
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,840
Class is over, and you're still grading?

250
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:59,560
Why? Did you come in last
in the competition?

251
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:00,680
The results aren't out yet.

252
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:09,280
Chen Huimei once said

253
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:11,920
that every competition is
a battle of mindset.

254
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:14,680
If your mindset is weak,
your opponents will seize the opportunity.

255
00:22:14,760 --> 00:22:17,800
If your mindset is strong,
your opponents will start to panic.

256
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,640
The results aren't even out yet.

257
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:21,240
Why do you look like you've already lost?

258
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:24,640
What competitions have you entered?

259
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:27,480
There are way too many.

260
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:30,240
Rubber-band jumping, shuttlecock-kicking,

261
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:33,240
competitive eating, skipping…

262
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:34,560
That's all for today's session.

263
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:44,280
About the Lantern Festival,

264
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:45,840
will you reconsider?

265
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,120
No.

266
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:04,680
PLAN WISELY, SUCCEED SMOOTHLY

267
00:23:12,160 --> 00:23:16,320
We have too many Lunar New Year supplies.
My parents said to bring Gao Xing some.

268
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:20,280
The tutoring session is over.
You can go in.

269
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:31,360
What? You've changed your mind?

270
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,680
Ms. Zheng.

271
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:36,960
Ms. Zheng Yu.

272
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:38,840
Zheng Yu.

273
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:41,040
Ms. Zheng!

274
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:50,960
THREE MEALS, FOUR SEASONS
WARM AND JOYFUL

275
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:02,280
Sir!

276
00:24:13,600 --> 00:24:14,800
Excuse me.

277
00:24:22,520 --> 00:24:23,680
What's up?

278
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:32,400
On the day of the presentation,

279
00:24:32,480 --> 00:24:35,280
you asked if I'd be disappointed
if we didn't win anything.

280
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:37,400
I haven't answered you yet.

281
00:24:44,040 --> 00:24:45,120
If we don't win,

282
00:24:45,720 --> 00:24:46,920
I won't be disappointed.

283
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:48,960
I'll just think the judges have no taste.

284
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:53,560
If we disagree with the results,
we can appeal to the organizing committee.

285
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:55,920
If our appeal is rejected,

286
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:59,080
we will revise our paper
and submit it for publication again.

287
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:03,160
Either way, the work we've done
and the effort we've put in

288
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:04,600
won't go to waste just like that.

289
00:25:09,160 --> 00:25:11,200
If we don't win any prizes,

290
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:14,480
the Campus Forum will probably
be flooded with posts again.

291
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:19,240
Are you worried about me?

292
00:25:30,040 --> 00:25:31,960
It's not like
this is the only project I'm doing.

293
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:34,920
I'll have plenty of chances
to shut them up.

294
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:39,720
Actually…

295
00:26:22,200 --> 00:26:24,800
Did you get on the wrong bus?
This one doesn't go to the campus.

296
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:28,040
Are you going to the university?

297
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:30,240
I'm going to the lab.

298
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:32,200
I'm not going that way.

299
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:34,160
I'm going to the hospital.

300
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:58,200
Just hold it right here.

301
00:27:04,120 --> 00:27:05,360
Keep your receipt.

302
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:08,800
Next.

303
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:16,080
INCOMING CALL

304
00:27:23,120 --> 00:27:25,040
<i>Well? Have you thought it through?</i>

305
00:27:26,960 --> 00:27:28,760
<i>If you're worried I'll go back on my word,</i>

306
00:27:28,840 --> 00:27:31,600
<i>I can transfer a 25,000 deposit</i>
<i>to you right now.</i>

307
00:27:33,720 --> 00:27:35,040
<i>Chen Huimei once said</i>

308
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:37,520
<i>that every competition is</i>
<i>a battle of mindset.</i>

309
00:27:37,600 --> 00:27:40,480
<i>If your mindset is weak,</i>
<i>your opponents will seize the opportunity.</i>

310
00:27:40,560 --> 00:27:43,320
<i>If your mindset is strong,</i>
<i>your opponents will start to panic.</i>

311
00:27:57,680 --> 00:27:59,640
RECENT CALLS, ZHENG YU

312
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:09,920
I wasn't looking at my phone earlier.
What happened?

313
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:11,400
<i>I'm almost at the lab building.</i>

314
00:28:11,480 --> 00:28:12,600
<i>Let's meet at the usual spot.</i>

315
00:28:12,680 --> 00:28:13,640
Sure.

316
00:28:24,640 --> 00:28:27,240
Three, two, one.

317
00:28:57,280 --> 00:28:59,520
The motion sensor light here
is unreliable.

318
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:01,080
Knocking on the railing works better.

319
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:17,920
So much has happened in just two days.

320
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:22,600
What did you tell him in the end?

321
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:24,560
I said

322
00:29:24,640 --> 00:29:26,080
I'd think it over

323
00:29:26,160 --> 00:29:28,920
and give him an answer by noon tomorrow.

324
00:29:30,520 --> 00:29:33,440
He was literally crying poor to you
at the coffee shop last time.

325
00:29:34,120 --> 00:29:35,440
How did he suddenly get so generous,

326
00:29:35,520 --> 00:29:38,200
trying to throw money around
to humiliate people now?

327
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:40,680
Unless…

328
00:29:40,760 --> 00:29:43,960
Unless, after making
this one generous offer,

329
00:29:44,040 --> 00:29:45,360
he stands to make even more money.

330
00:29:46,560 --> 00:29:48,320
You think he took money
from other contestants?

331
00:29:49,600 --> 00:29:51,480
If it weren't for that phone call today,

332
00:29:51,560 --> 00:29:53,200
I wouldn't have known
how desperate he was.

333
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:57,040
We should report to the university.

334
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:00,920
Without evidence,
they might not get involved.

335
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:04,040
We could've made a case out of
Cai Ronggen hitting someone,

336
00:30:04,120 --> 00:30:05,560
but I signed the settlement agreement.

337
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:07,480
Bringing it up now won't do much good.

338
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:14,600
- Do you know Ye Sheng?
- The boss of NingSheng BioTech?

339
00:30:16,120 --> 00:30:18,960
If I knew her,
I wouldn't be in this predicament.

340
00:30:21,120 --> 00:30:24,920
I saw a photo of you and her
in the counselor's office.

341
00:30:28,280 --> 00:30:29,320
How is that possible?

342
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:34,280
WELFARE PROJECT: HELPING UNDERPRIVILEGED
STUDENTS REALIZE THEIR DREAMS

343
00:30:49,680 --> 00:30:50,600
<i>Hello?</i>

344
00:30:52,520 --> 00:30:54,200
I've been thinking these past few days.

345
00:30:55,040 --> 00:30:56,880
If you'd been the one on stage,

346
00:30:57,840 --> 00:31:00,600
would Cai Ronggen have left us alone?

347
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:03,120
Because you just don't look like

348
00:31:03,760 --> 00:31:05,840
the kind of person
who'd be swayed by money.

349
00:31:10,880 --> 00:31:12,240
I know what I need to do now.

350
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:41,480
Hello, how can I help you?

351
00:31:43,680 --> 00:31:46,680
- Hello. I'd like to see Ms. Ye Sheng.
- Do you have an appointment?

352
00:31:49,080 --> 00:31:50,480
Then I'm afraid I can't assist you.

353
00:31:50,560 --> 00:31:52,240
Please schedule an appointment first.

354
00:31:52,320 --> 00:31:55,160
Could you call Ms. Ye for me?
I'd like to speak with her directly.

355
00:31:55,240 --> 00:31:58,080
It's currently lunch break,
so we can't disturb her right now.

356
00:32:03,280 --> 00:32:05,160
I'm a student at Qing Yi University.

357
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:07,800
Two years ago,
I received financial support from her.

358
00:32:07,880 --> 00:32:11,000
She told me if I ever ran into trouble,
I could come here to see her.

359
00:32:12,960 --> 00:32:14,760
Please wait a moment. I'll call and check.

360
00:32:25,200 --> 00:32:27,520
Is Mr. Cai Ronggen not in today?

361
00:32:27,600 --> 00:32:30,520
He is. But he's probably having lunch
in the canteen at this hour.

362
00:32:30,600 --> 00:32:32,240
You have a canteen here?

363
00:32:32,320 --> 00:32:33,600
We do. It's on the first floor.

364
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:36,560
Our company canteen is famous around here.

365
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:37,520
This way, please.

366
00:32:44,480 --> 00:32:45,600
Please come in.

367
00:32:46,480 --> 00:32:47,520
All right.

368
00:32:48,240 --> 00:32:49,520
I'm listening.

369
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:56,640
We still need to discuss
some of the details.

370
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:01,560
You name the time.

371
00:33:01,640 --> 00:33:02,800
Great.

372
00:33:03,760 --> 00:33:04,680
It's a deal then.

373
00:33:04,760 --> 00:33:05,960
Goodbye.

374
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:07,800
Hello, Ms. Ye.

375
00:33:07,880 --> 00:33:10,040
I'm Zheng Yu,
a student in the College of Life Sciences.

376
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:12,360
I remember you.

377
00:33:12,440 --> 00:33:13,680
Have a seat.

378
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:17,280
I visited your campus two years ago

379
00:33:17,360 --> 00:33:20,400
for the Corporate Scholarship
Award Ceremony.

380
00:33:20,480 --> 00:33:22,760
The outstanding
student representatives there

381
00:33:22,840 --> 00:33:24,400
weren't very keen to take photos with me.

382
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:27,200
You were the first person
to come up and take a photo with me.

383
00:33:27,840 --> 00:33:30,480
You brought your own
photography crew along back then.

384
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:33,280
The whole spectacle
scared all the students off.

385
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:35,440
They were afraid of ending up
on the front page.

386
00:33:35,520 --> 00:33:38,600
They weren't photographers.
They were my PR team.

387
00:33:39,160 --> 00:33:40,440
When I sponsor students' tuition,

388
00:33:40,520 --> 00:33:43,600
I genuinely hope to help those
who aren't as fortunate.

389
00:33:43,680 --> 00:33:45,000
I mean that sincerely.

390
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:51,920
I also hope my company can
build a good public image.

391
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:53,480
I mean that sincerely too.

392
00:33:53,560 --> 00:33:56,240
Those two goals don't have to conflict.

393
00:33:58,160 --> 00:34:01,880
But I never said you could come look for
me here whenever you had trouble.

394
00:34:03,760 --> 00:34:04,760
Recently,

395
00:34:04,840 --> 00:34:07,360
I participated in the Excellence Cup
sponsored by your company.

396
00:34:07,960 --> 00:34:10,040
- I made it to the finals.
- Is that so?

397
00:34:10,719 --> 00:34:11,840
Congratulations.

398
00:34:14,679 --> 00:34:17,440
Unfortunately, I had something come up
that day, so I couldn't attend.

399
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:22,880
Very unfortunate.

400
00:34:25,840 --> 00:34:26,840
What do you mean?

401
00:34:31,639 --> 00:34:33,400
Since you value
your company's image so much,

402
00:34:33,480 --> 00:34:36,239
you definitely wouldn't
allow this to happen.

403
00:34:36,320 --> 00:34:37,400
So

404
00:34:38,080 --> 00:34:40,000
you're not just helping me.

405
00:34:40,080 --> 00:34:41,960
Didn't you say

406
00:34:42,040 --> 00:34:45,639
you sincerely hoped
to help those who weren't as fortunate

407
00:34:46,239 --> 00:34:47,280
two years ago?

408
00:34:48,400 --> 00:34:50,600
And now,
as someone who received your help,

409
00:34:50,679 --> 00:34:51,800
I'm sitting here

410
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:53,840
with the same sincerity.

411
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:06,600
CAI RONGGEN

412
00:35:07,560 --> 00:35:09,520
<i>Have you made up your mind?</i>

413
00:35:12,120 --> 00:35:14,120
CAI RONGGEN

414
00:35:25,080 --> 00:35:26,840
<i>Something came up.</i>
<i>We'll talk later.</i>

415
00:35:33,280 --> 00:35:34,240
Mr. Zhang.

416
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:36,400
Mr. Cai, what bad timing.

417
00:35:36,480 --> 00:35:38,120
I just made plans with Xiaowang.

418
00:35:38,200 --> 00:35:40,960
We need to quickly go over
this afternoon's data report.

419
00:35:41,520 --> 00:35:42,800
Always so busy!

420
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:44,320
Not at all.

421
00:35:44,400 --> 00:35:46,120
It's all thanks to Ms. Ye's leadership.

422
00:35:46,200 --> 00:35:48,840
She has high standards,
so we can't afford to slack off.

423
00:35:49,440 --> 00:35:50,560
That's true.

424
00:35:50,640 --> 00:35:53,600
Ms. Ye's drive
for perfection is truly rare.

425
00:35:53,680 --> 00:35:54,560
That's for sure.

426
00:35:55,520 --> 00:35:57,280
That's what you get with a female boss.

427
00:35:57,960 --> 00:35:59,520
Women nowadays are different.

428
00:35:59,600 --> 00:36:00,840
They're impressive.

429
00:36:01,760 --> 00:36:03,000
I'll let you get back to work.

430
00:36:03,080 --> 00:36:04,680
All right, take care.

431
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:33,280
You shouldn't be here.

432
00:36:34,720 --> 00:36:36,720
When you proposed that deal,

433
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:38,240
did you never expect me to come here?

434
00:36:39,640 --> 00:36:41,840
It seems you no longer want the money.

435
00:36:43,480 --> 00:36:45,000
I'd rather win the prize money.

436
00:36:46,680 --> 00:36:48,760
You really think you can win the prize?

437
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:52,480
Fine.

438
00:36:52,560 --> 00:36:54,000
Let's wait for the results then.

439
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:56,960
Wait for what results?

440
00:36:57,720 --> 00:36:59,760
Wait for you to return
the bribe money you took

441
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:03,320
and act like nothing ever happened?

442
00:37:10,360 --> 00:37:11,840
I have no idea what you're talking about.

443
00:37:13,120 --> 00:37:15,800
How much did you sell the grand prize for?

444
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:31,000
RECENT CALLS, ZHENG YU

445
00:37:35,760 --> 00:37:38,360
<i>The number you have dialed</i>
<i>is currently busy.</i>

446
00:37:41,280 --> 00:37:43,040
So you're saying

447
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:45,960
I want to trick you into
withdrawing for free,

448
00:37:46,040 --> 00:37:47,880
and then make a huge profit
off someone else?

449
00:37:47,960 --> 00:37:49,080
Don't you?

450
00:37:49,640 --> 00:37:50,880
You're just gambling

451
00:37:51,720 --> 00:37:54,200
on how far someone like me,
who could be bought,

452
00:37:54,280 --> 00:37:56,320
would go for money.

453
00:38:00,240 --> 00:38:01,920
Which student paid you off?

454
00:38:02,760 --> 00:38:04,480
If our team withdraws,

455
00:38:04,560 --> 00:38:06,520
that person gets the grand prize.

456
00:38:08,440 --> 00:38:09,480
No. 16?

457
00:38:10,640 --> 00:38:12,000
No. 21?

458
00:38:12,080 --> 00:38:14,040
Or…

459
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:16,600
No. 7?

460
00:38:21,880 --> 00:38:22,960
Say whatever you want.

461
00:38:23,040 --> 00:38:24,480
No one's going to believe you anyway.

462
00:38:25,080 --> 00:38:26,120
Leave now.

463
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:27,760
If you don't leave, I'm calling security.

464
00:38:35,400 --> 00:38:36,560
Wait!

465
00:38:38,960 --> 00:38:39,800
Take out your phone.

466
00:38:44,080 --> 00:38:44,920
YE SHENG

467
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:46,120
<i>Cai Ronggen.</i>

468
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:50,840
Ms. Ye.

469
00:38:50,920 --> 00:38:53,880
You've heard everything you need to hear.
I'll hang up now.

470
00:38:59,480 --> 00:39:00,320
Mr. Cai.

471
00:39:01,520 --> 00:39:03,440
I'm afraid you won't be
presenting our prizes.

472
00:39:05,720 --> 00:39:06,600
What a pity.

473
00:39:39,120 --> 00:39:42,760
Hello, have you seen a girl
carrying a crossbody bag

474
00:39:42,840 --> 00:39:44,720
and wearing a green coat come upstairs?

475
00:39:44,800 --> 00:39:45,680
I did.

476
00:39:45,760 --> 00:39:47,640
My colleague was the one who helped her.

477
00:39:47,720 --> 00:39:49,720
She's probably eating
in the canteen right now.

478
00:39:50,600 --> 00:39:51,720
Then could you…

479
00:39:51,800 --> 00:39:53,080
Something happened over there!

480
00:39:53,160 --> 00:39:54,800
Mr. Cai got into a fight with a girl.

481
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:56,680
- Is it true?
- Yes.

482
00:39:56,760 --> 00:39:57,720
Seriously?

483
00:39:57,800 --> 00:39:58,800
Everyone.

484
00:39:59,360 --> 00:40:00,920
Please stay calm.

485
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:03,200
Today, I'm going to show you all

486
00:40:03,280 --> 00:40:06,080
a perfect example
of shameless, despicable behavior.

487
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:09,720
This woman is a student
from Qing Yi University.

488
00:40:09,800 --> 00:40:13,880
She entered the Excellence Cup
sponsored by our company.

489
00:40:13,960 --> 00:40:17,320
To win the prize, she tried bribing me
with money and gifts.

490
00:40:17,400 --> 00:40:19,360
Today, she showed up in person.

491
00:40:19,440 --> 00:40:22,200
I think you can all guess what she wanted.

492
00:40:22,280 --> 00:40:23,960
I don't need to spell it out, do I?

493
00:40:24,040 --> 00:40:26,120
When she failed to seduce me,

494
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:27,600
she threatened me.

495
00:40:27,680 --> 00:40:29,800
She said that
unless I gave the prize to her team,

496
00:40:29,880 --> 00:40:31,440
she'd report me for taking bribes!

497
00:40:31,520 --> 00:40:35,840
So I'd like to ask all of you
to serve as witnesses

498
00:40:35,920 --> 00:40:37,080
and testify that I'm innocent!

499
00:40:37,160 --> 00:40:38,200
Thank you, everyone!

500
00:40:39,920 --> 00:40:41,800
My goodness!

501
00:40:51,320 --> 00:40:52,840
Water!

502
00:40:52,920 --> 00:40:54,240
Get me some water!

503
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:56,080
Water! Hurry, get me water!

504
00:40:57,560 --> 00:40:58,560
<i>What's that smell?</i>

505
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:03,680
Water…

506
00:41:03,760 --> 00:41:05,240
Get me some water!

507
00:41:05,320 --> 00:41:06,720
Water! Hurry, get me water!

508
00:41:09,040 --> 00:41:10,840
Water! Hurry up!

509
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:12,400
This… Okay, thank you.

510
00:41:18,400 --> 00:41:22,160
Even though the liquor isn't that strong,
it can at least disinfect a little.

511
00:42:06,560 --> 00:42:09,240
Do you think Ye Sheng
will take care of this?

512
00:42:10,320 --> 00:42:11,160
She will.

513
00:42:12,200 --> 00:42:13,160
How are you so sure?

514
00:42:14,120 --> 00:42:14,960
Intuition.

515
00:42:20,600 --> 00:42:21,600
Did you ever hesitate?

516
00:42:26,000 --> 00:42:28,920
If I'd entered the competition alone,

517
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:30,720
I would've demanded even more money.

518
00:42:37,640 --> 00:42:38,560
Then

519
00:42:39,240 --> 00:42:40,840
it's a good thing you're not alone.

520
00:42:58,560 --> 00:43:01,280
I still have work to do.
Clean up when you're done eating.

521
00:43:01,360 --> 00:43:02,200
Okay.

522
00:43:06,640 --> 00:43:07,960
Let me do it.

523
00:43:08,800 --> 00:43:11,080
You were so quiet at dinner,
but now you're all eager to help.

524
00:43:12,240 --> 00:43:15,120
You seem to be in a good mood.
Could you do me a small favor?

525
00:43:16,560 --> 00:43:17,400
You guessed wrong.

526
00:43:17,480 --> 00:43:21,440
Help me convince Ms. Zheng
to take me out for the Lantern Festival.

527
00:43:22,520 --> 00:43:23,360
Where do you want to go?

528
00:43:23,440 --> 00:43:24,800
Anywhere is fine.

529
00:43:24,880 --> 00:43:27,760
School starts soon.
It'll be too late if I don't go now.

530
00:43:32,480 --> 00:43:34,680
I have a way to get her to agree.

531
00:43:34,760 --> 00:43:37,400
But you have to agree to one condition.

532
00:43:39,960 --> 00:43:42,640
These are the spots where you repeatedly
get the answers wrong.

533
00:43:42,720 --> 00:43:44,040
You need to review them thoroughly.

534
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:57,440
Life…

535
00:44:00,440 --> 00:44:04,400
<i>The field practice we postponed</i>
<i>last summer due to base maintenance</i>

536
00:44:04,480 --> 00:44:07,360
<i>will take place one week before</i>
<i>the start of this semester.</i>

537
00:44:14,960 --> 00:44:16,040
Lesson's over.

538
00:44:38,320 --> 00:44:39,800
Bringing Lunar New Year supplies again?

539
00:44:42,160 --> 00:44:43,320
I need to talk to you.

540
00:44:45,440 --> 00:44:46,800
I knew it.

541
00:44:46,880 --> 00:44:49,800
The Lantern Festival is coming up,
and she's been unusually quiet.

542
00:44:49,880 --> 00:44:51,560
Turns out she got you to lobby me.

543
00:44:53,480 --> 00:44:55,440
I've thought of plenty of reasons
to convince you.

544
00:44:56,640 --> 00:44:57,840
For example?

545
00:44:58,640 --> 00:45:00,240
For example…

546
00:45:00,320 --> 00:45:02,760
Gao Xing has been studying for so long.
She needs a break.

547
00:45:03,360 --> 00:45:06,080
Her mom couldn't even come home
for the holidays,

548
00:45:06,160 --> 00:45:07,960
and her dad has started a new life.

549
00:45:08,040 --> 00:45:10,440
As her tutor, you should look out for her.

550
00:45:11,040 --> 00:45:14,640
If you're worried her mom might object,
I can handle that.

551
00:45:17,000 --> 00:45:19,520
So which reason are you going with?

552
00:45:23,440 --> 00:45:24,880
The break is almost over.

553
00:45:26,080 --> 00:45:27,680
Do you want to go out and have fun?

554
00:45:31,720 --> 00:45:32,760
Where to?

555
00:45:33,840 --> 00:45:34,880
Where do you want to go?

556
00:45:36,560 --> 00:45:37,760
I don't know.

557
00:45:39,200 --> 00:45:40,040
Think about it.

558
00:45:42,520 --> 00:45:43,520
The rollerblading rink.

559
00:45:45,440 --> 00:45:47,920
Why the rollerblading rink?

560
00:45:50,200 --> 00:45:52,320
I don't know what fun places
there are in Qingyi.

561
00:45:53,080 --> 00:45:56,920
<i>Now the PE class is over, I haven't</i>
<i>had time to do any rollerblading.</i>

562
00:46:00,160 --> 00:46:02,320
RECALL MESSAGE

563
00:46:04,840 --> 00:46:05,800
Wait.

564
00:46:05,880 --> 00:46:07,480
Did you see that message I sent?

565
00:46:08,560 --> 00:46:10,240
Why didn't you reply?

566
00:46:10,320 --> 00:46:11,480
You withdrew the message.

567
00:46:11,560 --> 00:46:12,880
What was there to reply to?

568
00:46:14,640 --> 00:46:16,800
Then let's go to the rollerblading rink.

569
00:46:16,880 --> 00:46:18,040
I'm not going there.

570
00:46:19,160 --> 00:46:21,680
Then where do you want to go?
We'll go wherever you want.

571
00:46:23,240 --> 00:46:24,440
Anywhere but there.

572
00:46:25,320 --> 00:46:26,640
Why are you walking so fast?

573
00:46:27,800 --> 00:46:30,800
By the way,
I'm planning to submit my paper.

574
00:46:30,880 --> 00:46:32,120
You're finally submitting it?

575
00:46:33,080 --> 00:46:34,160
Going out and having fun?

576
00:46:34,240 --> 00:46:36,160
Sounds like you're the one
who wants a break.

577
00:46:53,360 --> 00:46:55,400
FORTUNE

578
00:46:59,960 --> 00:47:01,520
Ms. Zheng, give me a smile.

579
00:47:02,600 --> 00:47:03,840
Come on, just smile.

580
00:47:03,920 --> 00:47:04,840
Please?

581
00:47:15,200 --> 00:47:16,280
I'll go get my bag.

582
00:47:16,800 --> 00:47:19,760
We're going out, yeah!

583
00:47:24,200 --> 00:47:27,160
You didn't tell her
that her mom knew we were going out?

584
00:47:28,560 --> 00:47:30,640
Okay, let's go, let's go!

585
00:47:32,880 --> 00:47:33,720
Let's go!

586
00:47:34,680 --> 00:47:35,840
Let's go.

587
00:47:58,280 --> 00:47:59,440
Have you ever been to the beach?

588
00:48:02,240 --> 00:48:03,640
I went when I was little.

589
00:48:04,760 --> 00:48:06,000
Qingyi is a coastal city.

590
00:48:06,080 --> 00:48:09,040
It's only a 50 or 60-minute drive
from the campus to the beach.

591
00:48:09,800 --> 00:48:12,160
You've been here so long,
and you've never gone?

592
00:48:15,360 --> 00:48:16,640
Then make the most of it today.

593
00:48:31,760 --> 00:48:34,240
I can't hear a thing. Keep talking.

594
00:49:17,240 --> 00:49:18,640
What's in your bag?

595
00:49:18,720 --> 00:49:19,640
It's so heavy.

596
00:49:24,640 --> 00:49:26,280
This is a mirrorless camera.

597
00:49:26,360 --> 00:49:27,920
This is a film camera.

598
00:49:28,000 --> 00:49:29,680
And this is a CCD camera.

599
00:49:29,760 --> 00:49:31,400
Are you setting up a camera stall?

600
00:49:31,480 --> 00:49:33,000
Of course not!

601
00:49:33,760 --> 00:49:35,840
I just want to try each one out.

602
00:49:35,920 --> 00:49:38,680
Chen Huimei usually
doesn't have time to take me out,

603
00:49:38,760 --> 00:49:40,080
so I rarely use them.

604
00:49:40,160 --> 00:49:43,000
I'm going to fill them all up
with photos today.

605
00:49:47,120 --> 00:49:48,760
There's a luggage storage place
back there.

606
00:49:48,840 --> 00:49:51,440
Keep one camera with you
and leave the rest there.

607
00:49:51,520 --> 00:49:54,320
- Be good.
- Fine. It is a bit heavy.

608
00:50:10,520 --> 00:50:12,680
Look. There's a little island over there.

609
00:50:18,360 --> 00:50:19,600
Doesn't it look familiar?

610
00:50:20,760 --> 00:50:21,920
I've never been here before.

611
00:50:22,000 --> 00:50:23,280
How would it look familiar?

612
00:50:40,440 --> 00:50:42,160
Then where did you get this photo?

613
00:50:43,440 --> 00:50:44,920
I saw it online.

614
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:47,240
I thought it was beautiful, so I saved it.

615
00:50:48,440 --> 00:50:51,840
It seems beautiful places
aren't always far away.

616
00:51:04,400 --> 00:51:05,960
Hurry up.

617
00:51:22,720 --> 00:51:23,600
I'll do it.

618
00:51:45,680 --> 00:51:46,760
Here we go!

619
00:52:15,920 --> 00:52:18,800
You both had your eyes closed
when the photo was taken.

620
00:52:18,880 --> 00:52:22,840
But since you two brought me out for fun,

621
00:52:22,920 --> 00:52:25,720
I'll be generous
and let you take up my memory space.

622
00:52:29,360 --> 00:52:30,400
Move closer together.

623
00:52:30,480 --> 00:52:31,720
You're out of the frame.

624
00:52:40,160 --> 00:52:41,480
A little closer!

625
00:52:52,320 --> 00:52:53,160
Three.

626
00:52:54,080 --> 00:52:54,920
Two.

627
00:52:56,000 --> 00:52:56,840
One.

628
00:53:03,560 --> 00:53:06,760
<i>Sometimes, I feel like</i>
<i>I live in a world of gray.</i>

629
00:53:06,840 --> 00:53:09,080
<i>Not the dirty kind of gray,</i>

630
00:53:09,160 --> 00:53:12,640
<i>but the kind where debt</i>
<i>is a bottomless pit</i>

631
00:53:12,720 --> 00:53:14,680
<i>and part-time jobs never end.</i>

632
00:53:15,840 --> 00:53:17,480
<i>Life feels so thin.</i>

633
00:53:17,560 --> 00:53:18,560
<i>So light.</i>

634
00:53:19,360 --> 00:53:20,960
<i>It makes no sound as it falls.</i>

635
00:53:21,600 --> 00:53:22,560
Zheng Yu.

636
00:53:22,640 --> 00:53:24,960
<i>But he's the kind of person</i>
<i>who blows the gray away,</i>

637
00:53:25,640 --> 00:53:27,320
<i>pulls you out of it,</i>

638
00:53:28,120 --> 00:53:29,920
<i>and takes you out to waste a little time.</i>

639
00:53:31,000 --> 00:53:32,640
<i>And that little bit of time</i>

640
00:53:33,520 --> 00:53:35,480
<i>is just enough to make life</i>

641
00:53:35,560 --> 00:53:37,680
<i>feel breathable again.</i>

642
00:56:05,720 --> 00:56:10,720
Subtitle translation by: Cempaka Malinja
